     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg per day (immediate-release, in divided doses). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum single dose of about 1,000 \u043a\u0430\u0440\u0442 mg. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nHere are a few things you may have meant:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg per day and the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If 1,700 mg three times daily is really what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was verified. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
